        "original_id": "a3856145-6f5e-5a33-88d9-8617e63d61a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Sunday Driver, Madrugada, MonstrO\n- Albums: Live at Tralfamadore, Madrugada\n- Music scenes: UK Steampunk scene\n- People: Bevan Davies, Kyle Sanders, Juan Montoya, Charlie Suarez\n\nFacts:\n- On 21 January 2008, Madrugada released the album \"Madrugada\" and announced that the band would split after one last tour.\n- On 15 November 2008, Madrugada performed its final concert.\n- In 2009, Sunday Driver became popular within the UK Steampunk scene.\n- Live at Tralfamadore is the fifth album and the first live album by the Norwegian band Madrugada.\n- MonstrO is an alternative band composed of Bevan Davies, Kyle Sanders, Juan Montoya, and Charlie Suarez.\n- Bevan Davies had previously been the drummer for Still Rain, Danzig, and Bloodsimple before joining MonstrO.\n- Kyle Sanders had previously been the bassist for Bloodsimple, Medication, and Skrew before joining MonstrO.\n- Juan Montoya had previously been the guitarist for Torche before joining MonstrO.\n- Charlie Suarez had previously been a guitarist and vocalist for Sunday Driver before joining MonstrO.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
